desktop-shell, clipboard: maximize/restore on the right screen; paste text from any app

Several screens:
- Maximizing a minimized window (taskbar menu) put it on the primary
  screen: a minimized view is on no shown layer, so surface->output is
  NULL and Weston fell back to the default output. The window's screen
  now comes from its position and size, which also works when minimized.
- Restoring a window that opened maximized (no saved position) put it
  on the screen under the pointer, e.g. the taskbar used to restore it.
  It is now centered on the screen it was maximized on, as is a window
  whose saved place is on no screen any more.
- Taskbar "Maximize" brings the window back from minimized before
  maximizing it, not after.

Clipboard: the clipboard manager kept and offered only the first MIME
type of a copy. Chromium/Electron programs (VS Code) list text/html or
their own types first, so once the copy was taken over, a terminal
(foot), asking for plain text, had nothing to paste. It now keeps plain
text (UTF-8 when offered) and offers it under the usual text names, and
frees all the type names it keeps.
---
